# What must not travel inside the packed .mcpb.
#
# `mcpb pack` does not read .gitignore. It applies its own built-in exclusion
# list (.git, node_modules/.cache, *.log, .env*, ...) plus this file, and it
# treats .gitignore itself as just another file to leave out. So every path
# that .gitignore protects has to be repeated here or it ships.

# Real personal health exports: Apple Health, Garmin, and anything derived from
# them. Packing these would publish a real person's health record inside an
# extension that other people install. This entry is the reason the file exists.
data/private/

# Read by tests and import scripts, never on the server's import path.
data/vendor/
schemas/

# Tests.
**/test/
*.test.js

# Development surface: none of it is reachable from the entry point.
docs/
eval/
# The decision harness, and the fixed evidence it runs on. Invented readings for
# an invented athlete, but they are shaped exactly like a real person's health
# record — and this list exists because that shape, not its truth, is what must
# not travel inside something other people install.
harness/
scripts/
# Demo prompts and sample evidence. They are read by a person on GitHub before
# installing, not by the server after it — evidence arrives as call arguments,
# so nothing here is ever loaded from disk at runtime.
examples/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Source. The bundle runs dist/evidra-server.mjs, which `npm run build:bundle`
# compiles from these two trees — shipping them as well would put the same code
# in the archive twice, once readable. `packages/rules/data/session-rules.json`
# goes with them: the build inlines it into the bundle as a string, so nothing
# under packages/ is read at runtime.
#
# This does not make the rules private. Every decision returns the governing
# rule's thresholds and citations in `decisionBasis`; the archive is simply no
# longer the easy way to read them.
apps/
packages/

# esbuild, and nothing the server imports. The bundle has no runtime deps.
node_modules/

# Registry metadata, and it cannot be packed. Its `fileSha256` is the hash of
# the archive itself, so an archive containing it can never agree with it:
# filling the field changes the hash that the field states. The registry reads
# this file from the repository, and no code reads it at runtime.
server.json

# The packed archive itself, which lands in dist/ beside the compiled server.
*.mcpb

# Screen recordings and screenshots. A 28MB .mcpb caught one of these already:
# a recording of the extension being used, which is a recording of someone's
# health data, packed into a file other people install. Nothing here is ever
# part of the extension, so the rule is by extension rather than by name.
*.mov
*.mp4
*.png
!icon.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif

# Kept: manifest.json, README.md (the submission requires its Privacy Policy
# section to travel with the bundle), package.json (the server reads its
# version), release-manifest.json (the runtime identity), dist/, and data/seeds + data/fixtures, which the server reads at
# runtime through knowledgeBase.js and demoData.js.
